# The tutorial's board (apple2/draw/tutorial.c): a square is 5 bytes (35 pixels) by 32 lines, empty, with
# your X or with the partner's O. In color the square is green with a black gap round it, the X white and
# the O a black ring; in monochrome the square is an outline and the marks are drawn in single dots. A
# Hi-Res pixel is about 7/6 as tall as it is wide, so the marks are 26 pixels (13 color pixels) across and
# 22 lines down, which is square on a monitor, centered on the square. Color squares come in two (both): a
# square at an odd byte column starts on an odd pixel. Made for this program.

